---
import Shell from '../../layouts/Shell.astro';
import ArticleByline from '../../components/ArticleByline.astro';
import ArticleReadingPath from '../../components/ArticleReadingPath.astro';
import {cinema,picture} from '../../lib/cinema-article.mjs';
import '../../styles/article-reading.css';
const lead=cinema.articles[0],hero=lead.images.find(i=>i.role==='title');
const mb=n=>(n/1000000).toFixed(1)+' MB';
---
<Shell title="Odia Cinema: A Living Screen — the book" description="Download the connected digital and printable book about Odia cinema, literature, radio, television and the people making stories." active="explore" related={false} shareImage={{src:hero.file,alt:lead.hero.alt,width:hero.width,height:hero.height}}>
 <article class="article-reading cinema-book"><p><a href="/cinema/">← The cinema readings</a></p><h1>Odia Cinema:<br/>A Living Screen</h1><p>Stories, People and the Places Between</p><ArticleByline author="Ahimanikya Satapathy"/>
  <figure><Fragment set:html={picture(hero,lead.hero.alt,true)}/><figcaption>{lead.hero.caption}</figcaption></figure>
  <p>A connected reading edition in fourteen chapters: cinema and its shared voices, films and filmmakers, changing screens, and the conditions for making the next film. It includes children’s cinema and animation, literary passages, documentary images, source notes and viewing links.</p>
  <p>The current fourteen-chapter PDF edition predates the expanded online companion pages. The <a href="/cinema/">online reading collection</a> includes those later additions.</p>
  <h2>Choose your edition</h2><ul><li><a href="https://github.com/ahimanikya/project-odisha/releases/download/odia-cinema-book-2026-10-26/odia-cinema-a-living-screen.pdf">Digital reading edition — PDF, {mb(cinema.books[0].bytes)}</a>. Hosted as a Project Odisha release download. 95 pages, linked contents and sources.</li><li><a href="https://github.com/ahimanikya/project-odisha/releases/download/odia-cinema-book-2026-10-26/odia-cinema-a-living-screen-print.pdf">Printable reading edition — PDF download, {mb(cinema.books[1].bytes)}</a>. Hosted as a Project Odisha release download. 106 pages, mirrored margins, printed source URLs and high-resolution images.</li></ul>
  <h2>Printing the book</h2><p>The print edition uses a 6 × 9 inch page. Print at 100% on matching stock, duplex with long-edge binding, or ask a print shop to impose and trim it to that size. For A4 or Letter home printing, choose fit-to-page and expect a different finished size. This is a reading edition, not a printer-specific press-ready PDF.</p>
  <p>Edition reviewed 26 October 2026. Documentary images retain their credits and reuse terms; imagined illustrations are labelled. The book offers a sourced reading of this history, not a definitive account of every Odia film.</p>
  <ArticleReadingPath links={[{href:'/cinema/',title:'Read the connected articles online'},{href:'/cinema/watch/',title:'Open the viewing room',description:'Source-hosted films and clips, with provider conditions made explicit.'}]}/>
 </article>
</Shell>
<style>.cinema-book{max-width:804px;padding-inline:32px}.cinema-book :global(img){max-width:100%;height:auto}@media(max-width:600px){.cinema-book{padding-inline:22px}}</style>
